# Stop all agents = AI agents only (hard rule)

Operator directive (Phil, 2026-08-09):

> **When I say stop / pause / halt all agents, I always mean AI agents.**

## The rule

> **Phrases like “stop all agents,” “pause all agents,” “halt agents,” or
> “kill the agents” apply only to Cursor AI agents (this chat’s Task /
> Multitask children, and guidance to abandon / not spawn more). They do
> NOT mean kill shell PIDs, cargo builds, Playwright, `Deploy-*.ps1`,
> `npm run dev`, Windows services, Hyper-V VMs, or lab infrastructure —
> unless the operator names those processes or services in the same
> message.**

## Required agent behavior

1. **Stop AI work** — Do not spawn new `Task` / subagents. Do not resume
   stuck Multitask children. Interrupt only when acting as the owning
   parent per [`stuck-agent-supervisor.mdc`](stuck-agent-supervisor.mdc).
2. **Leave machine work alone** — Do not ask whether to kill deploys,
   Vite, cargo, or services as part of “stop agents.” Report them only
   if useful for a resume note; do not stop them.
3. **Resume lists** — When capturing work for later restart, list AI
   chats / agent IDs first. Background shells are optional context, not
   “agents that were stopped.”
4. **Explicit exception** — Only kill or stop non-AI processes when the
   same message names them (e.g. “stop all agents and kill the duplicate
   deploys”).

## Forbidden

- Treating “stop all agents” as permission to `Stop-Process` on deploy /
  build / dev-server PIDs.
- Stopping `aic-server-service` / agent services as part of an agents pause.
- Asking clarifying questions about killing background jobs when the only
  instruction was to stop agents (ask only if the operator also asked to
  clean up machine processes).

